WEBVTT

00:08.160 --> 00:09.790
The weather is nice again today!

00:09.790 --> 00:12.590
Sora! Should we go hunting today?

00:17.090 --> 00:19.120
Morning, Ivy. You're up early.

00:19.120 --> 00:21.950
Good morning! I thought I'd go hunting.

00:21.950 --> 00:23.840
I see. Well, be careful.

00:23.840 --> 00:26.060
I will! Thank you.

00:30.320 --> 00:31.840
Morning, Ivy!

00:31.840 --> 00:34.200
G-Good morning.

00:35.400 --> 00:37.890
Children should be energetic, like you, Ivy.

00:37.890 --> 00:39.890
Th-Thank you.

00:39.890 --> 00:42.180
Nice weather, isn't it, Ivy?

00:42.180 --> 00:43.770
Y-Yes, it is.

00:43.770 --> 00:46.460
I see you're already hard 
at work this morning, Ivy!

00:46.460 --> 00:47.650
You're too kind.

00:47.650 --> 00:50.050
Want some noberries, Ivy?

00:50.050 --> 00:51.530
Much obliged.

00:51.810 --> 00:54.320
E-Everyone knows who I am.

00:55.140 --> 00:56.610
But how?

00:57.380 --> 01:01.520
<i>When I'm alone, I can breathe</i>

01:01.520 --> 01:05.680
<i>In a world with no one 
but me, I feel at ease</i>

01:06.340 --> 01:10.700
<i>But I think the truth is</i>

01:10.700 --> 01:16.680
<i>That I've been waiting for 
morning's light to break through</i>

01:14.180 --> 01:22.440
<b>The Weakest Tamer
Began a Journey
to Pick Up Trash</b>

01:14.340 --> 01:16.680
<i>(Where could it be?)</i>

01:16.680 --> 01:19.930
<i>Beyond the edges of a yet unknown map</i>

01:19.930 --> 01:24.190
<i>That's where I'll find a place 
where I can live</i>

01:22.440 --> 01:24.190
<i>(If it exists...)</i>

01:24.190 --> 01:26.200
<i>I'd like to go there</i>

01:26.200 --> 01:29.950
<i>And with trembling legs, 
I take a step forward</i>

01:29.950 --> 01:32.540
<i>I'm on a journey without end</i>

01:32.540 --> 01:34.850
<i>And even if I carry nothing with me</i>

01:34.850 --> 01:37.000
<i>I'll take everything I feel</i>

01:37.000 --> 01:38.960
<i>And pack it into my once empty bag</i>

01:38.960 --> 01:40.780
<i>I'll go as far as I need to</i>

01:40.780 --> 01:43.000
<i>On this journey to find myself</i>

01:43.000 --> 01:45.090
<i>And everything I'm given along the way</i>

01:45.090 --> 01:49.550
<i>Will slowly fill my heart to the brim</i>

01:59.420 --> 02:03.780
<i>Now, I'm not all alone anymore</i>

02:03.780 --> 02:08.700
<i>Because I've met new, dear friends</i>

02:08.700 --> 02:13.450
<i>(Maybe we can understand each other 
because we're alike. Isn't it strange?)</i>

02:13.450 --> 02:16.660
<i>Your bright laughter gives me courage</i>

02:16.660 --> 02:20.920
<i>(I feel like I'm wrapped up 
snugly by your warmth)</i>

02:20.920 --> 02:26.170
<i>From now on, let's stay 
together forever and ever</i>

02:27.000 --> 02:32.010
<b>To Travel
Beyond Imagination</b>

02:35.260 --> 02:38.650
A nonoshi destroyed the trap again.

02:40.060 --> 02:43.060
We'll never catch anything at this rate.

02:43.060 --> 02:44.830
What do we do?

02:45.940 --> 02:49.760
I want to catch as much as I can during 
the summer so I can save up some money.

02:50.800 --> 02:53.890
What could this be? 
I sense an unusual presence.

02:53.890 --> 02:55.360
This is...

02:56.940 --> 02:58.240
Ciel!

03:02.660 --> 03:06.570
What? Are you giving them to me?

03:08.490 --> 03:11.580
You're so smart! Thank you!

03:12.750 --> 03:15.110
One, two, three, four...

03:15.440 --> 03:16.840
There's nine of them!

03:16.840 --> 03:20.800
And they're all completely intact. 
How did you catch them?

03:21.170 --> 03:22.720
Well, I'd better start dressing these!

03:22.720 --> 03:25.520
When you're selling meat, freshness 
is the most important thing!

03:33.580 --> 03:35.490
I'm done!

03:38.950 --> 03:40.770
Sora, wake up.

03:42.780 --> 03:45.700
We have to go sell the meat 
while it's still fresh.

03:51.830 --> 03:56.420
What? "Is Ciel really an adandala?"

03:58.410 --> 04:01.660
She looks just like 
the adandala in the book,

04:01.660 --> 04:03.990
but she isn't savage at all.

04:07.550 --> 04:12.440
Um... thank you for letting me 
have so much meat today!

04:17.650 --> 04:20.190
Well, we should head back now, too.

04:24.450 --> 04:27.200
Sora, you've gotten a lot stronger.

04:27.200 --> 04:30.300
You used to seem like you'd 
disappear at any moment.

04:34.630 --> 04:38.130
Although that clumsy side of you
 doesn't seem to have changed.

04:41.400 --> 04:44.250
It's very fresh, and the meat 
isn't gamey at all.

04:44.250 --> 04:46.880
You caught them without damaging 
the organs, didn't you?

04:46.880 --> 04:48.000
Did you use a trap?

04:48.000 --> 04:49.920
Um, yes!

04:49.920 --> 04:52.780
Really? They tend to struggle in traps, 
which degrades the flavor,

04:52.780 --> 04:54.140
but there's no sign of that either.

04:54.140 --> 04:55.230
How did you do it?

04:55.230 --> 04:57.590
Uh, well...

04:57.590 --> 05:00.450
Oh, is it a trade secret?

05:00.450 --> 05:02.700
For a child, you've got
a good head on your shoulders.

05:04.090 --> 05:06.660
They've been butchered very well. 
No problems here!

05:06.660 --> 05:10.800
One is worth 95 dal, so nine 
comes to 855 dal.

05:10.800 --> 05:12.120
Thank you!

05:12.120 --> 05:14.850
With this quality, you're more than welcome!

05:14.850 --> 05:17.090
If you catch any more, bring them by.

05:18.780 --> 05:20.550
I'm so glad I managed to sell them.

05:20.550 --> 05:22.830
Today is all thanks to Ciel.

05:22.830 --> 05:24.890
Did you make some good money, Ivy?

05:25.220 --> 05:27.430
Um, yes.

05:27.430 --> 05:29.840
There weren't any nonoshi, were there, Ivy?

05:29.840 --> 05:31.730
No, everything was fine.

05:32.140 --> 05:34.260
Did you catch something good to eat, Ivy?

05:34.260 --> 05:35.860
Yes, lots.

05:37.900 --> 05:43.200
Wh-Why? How do they all know who I am?

05:43.200 --> 05:44.720
Hey there, Ivy.

05:45.750 --> 05:47.250
Mister Vellivera?

05:47.960 --> 05:51.410
What's wrong? Why are you 
hiding in a place like this?

05:52.300 --> 05:56.240
Oh, he's already gotten that far?

05:56.240 --> 05:58.190
It's Captain Oggto.

05:58.190 --> 06:01.890
"If an adventurer named Ivy is in trouble, 
be sure to help him out."

06:01.890 --> 06:04.020
He's been saying that to all the watchmen.

06:04.020 --> 06:04.810
What?

06:04.810 --> 06:08.600
"He's young, but he's working hard, 
so please look out for him."

06:08.600 --> 06:09.640
What?!

06:10.010 --> 06:13.000
Once he gets an idea in his head, 
no one can stop him.

06:13.000 --> 06:14.610
I'm sorry if all this scared you.

06:14.610 --> 06:17.010
Not at all. It's all right.

06:17.010 --> 06:19.560
I'll have a word with Captain Oggto.

06:19.560 --> 06:21.980
But keep doing your best, Ivy.

06:21.980 --> 06:23.570
Y-Yes, sir!

06:27.600 --> 06:31.530
I appreciate the thought, 
but I don't like standing out.

06:31.960 --> 06:33.040
Still...

06:38.990 --> 06:41.340
this might be a good place!

06:45.300 --> 06:47.420
Oh! They have zaro!

06:47.420 --> 06:48.470
They're so expensive!

06:48.470 --> 06:50.070
The zaro fruit?

06:50.070 --> 06:53.020
It's taken me a long time 
to get my hands on those.

06:53.020 --> 06:55.480
Were these zaro picked in Latomi Village?

06:55.840 --> 06:58.860
Well, that's the only area 
where zaro can be grown.

06:58.860 --> 07:01.440
But it was a bad crop this year, 
so it's been a complete mess.

07:01.440 --> 07:03.440
Could it be that you're from Latomi Village?

07:03.440 --> 07:04.570
Yes.

07:04.570 --> 07:05.630
Where are your parents?

07:05.630 --> 07:08.410
Oh... I'm traveling on my own.

07:08.410 --> 07:11.290
I see. It's that idiot 
village head's fault, is it?

07:11.290 --> 07:12.490
The head?

07:12.830 --> 07:15.210
Did you leave the village 
without knowing anything?

07:15.210 --> 07:18.170
Or, wait... were you kicked out?

07:18.170 --> 07:20.170
No, I ran away.

07:20.170 --> 07:23.210
What's going on in Latomi Village right now?

07:23.210 --> 07:25.720
There was a fortune teller 
named Mistress Luba, right?

07:26.270 --> 07:27.720
Mistress Luba.

07:27.720 --> 07:31.440
Mistress Luba has always protected 
the zaro crops of Latomi Village.

07:31.440 --> 07:34.060
The harvest time for zaro fruit 
is always tricky.

07:34.060 --> 07:37.060
If you miss the timing, even by a little, 
they won't be fit to sell.

07:37.060 --> 07:41.020
That's why they had the fortune teller 
foretell the harvest's future.

07:41.340 --> 07:44.290
Zaro fruit is Latomi's source of income.

07:44.290 --> 07:47.430
That's why the villagers 
loved and respected Mistress Luba.

07:47.430 --> 07:51.430
But that idiot village head
 couldn't stand that.

07:51.430 --> 07:56.200
So, when Mistress Luba fell ill, he didn't 
give her any medicine. That's what they say.

07:56.910 --> 07:59.320
We've lost someone very precious.

07:59.320 --> 08:02.250
Who could imagine dying of a cold 
at this time of year?

08:02.680 --> 08:04.250
That can't be!

08:04.250 --> 08:08.180
And on top of everything, I heard 
he's trying to blame it all on a child.

08:08.180 --> 08:14.560
Fortune Teller Luba ignored my warnings 
and looked after the starless Femicia.

08:14.560 --> 08:19.810
Due to that, she received the curse of
 the starless, the ones forsaken by the gods!

08:21.660 --> 08:24.860
After losing their fortune 
teller so suddenly,

08:24.860 --> 08:29.200
Latomi Village's zaro harvest failed, 
and they fell into financial hardship,

08:29.200 --> 08:32.410
so the head has been trying to reduce 
the number of mouths to feed.

08:32.410 --> 08:36.330
Some of the villagers rebelled, 
took their families, and left the village.

08:36.330 --> 08:38.870
Others who defied the head 
were thrown out of the village.

08:38.870 --> 08:41.340
It's a complete disaster!

08:41.340 --> 08:43.590
Son, you said you ran away, didn't you?

08:43.930 --> 08:44.770
Yes...

08:44.770 --> 08:45.800
Why was that?

08:45.800 --> 08:49.760
My parents sided with the head... 
and that caused problems.

08:49.760 --> 08:52.470
I see. That must have been rough.

08:52.470 --> 08:55.650
It's all right. Thank you 
for telling me all of that.

08:57.710 --> 08:58.890
Take this with you.

08:59.340 --> 09:00.600
Are you sure?

09:00.600 --> 09:04.200
It's gotten overripe, so I can't sell it now.

09:04.200 --> 09:06.570
You must be facing a lot, 
but keep working hard.

09:06.570 --> 09:08.520
Thank you.

09:11.570 --> 09:14.250
I didn't know all that had 
happened in Latomi Village.

09:15.370 --> 09:20.710
Mom and Dad, my big brother and sister... 
I wonder what's happened to them.

09:22.810 --> 09:26.260
The village... my family cast me aside.

09:28.020 --> 09:31.920
I'm in an unfamiliar place 
with people I don't know.

09:32.510 --> 09:33.610
But...

09:35.130 --> 09:38.530
I've been cast aside, but I'm having fun now.

09:38.530 --> 09:40.890
I have you and Ciel.

09:40.890 --> 09:42.860
And I have Mister Oggto 
and Mister Vellivera...

09:42.860 --> 09:44.280
Lots of people are there for me.

09:44.280 --> 09:45.690
And everyone is so kind.

09:47.930 --> 09:51.110
That's true. I have my past life, too.

09:52.690 --> 09:54.990
It's small, but I even have a home now.

09:54.990 --> 09:58.220
Maybe this is what people call happiness.

10:00.760 --> 10:03.370
As usual, I have no idea what you're saying.

10:05.930 --> 10:07.950
I don't understand, but I understand.

10:07.950 --> 10:09.370
We're friends, after all!

10:14.830 --> 10:16.470
Yes. That's a zaro.

10:16.470 --> 10:18.830
That's the flavor I tasted when I was little.

10:18.830 --> 10:21.310
That's the flavor 
the fortune teller protected.

10:21.560 --> 10:24.460
Go to the town neighboring 
the royal capital.

10:24.460 --> 10:28.340
But if you find a place where you'd like to 
live forever while on your journey, do that.

10:28.340 --> 10:31.910
However, you must find people 
that you can trust.

10:31.910 --> 10:34.320
When you do, you must tell them everything.

10:35.320 --> 10:38.210
This flavor... I have to remember it.

10:43.590 --> 10:45.420
The weather's nice again today!

10:46.010 --> 10:47.290
Morning, Ivy.

10:48.100 --> 10:49.610
Good morning!

10:50.380 --> 10:51.860
Morning, Ivy!

10:51.860 --> 10:53.270
Good morning!

10:53.270 --> 10:55.170
Nice weather, isn't it, Ivy?

10:55.170 --> 10:57.640
Yes! The sun feels very nice!

10:57.640 --> 11:00.090
I see you're already hard 
at work this morning, Ivy!

11:00.090 --> 11:02.290
Yes! I'll do my very best again today!

11:12.060 --> 11:13.420
That should do it!

11:13.420 --> 11:15.740
I've set them in places 
the nonoshi won't step on them,

11:15.740 --> 11:17.260
so they should be fine this time.

11:19.200 --> 11:20.720
Now, let's head back.

11:20.720 --> 11:23.430
We have to go and gather your meal 
at the dumping ground.

11:27.760 --> 11:29.170
<i>I sense people.</i>

11:29.170 --> 11:30.130
Sora!

11:33.630 --> 11:36.940
What's this? If it isn't that kid 
from the other day.

11:36.940 --> 11:39.010
Fancy running into you here.

11:39.010 --> 11:41.710
You had some gall,
 doing what you did back there.

11:42.220 --> 11:44.190
I didn't do anything.

11:44.190 --> 11:47.850
I don't want to hear it! It's your fault 
my friend got arrested!

11:49.260 --> 11:52.650
Now that I think about it, 
you had a rare slime, didn't you?

11:54.060 --> 11:56.490
Hand it over, and I'll let you go.

11:56.490 --> 11:57.270
No.

11:57.270 --> 11:58.660
Huh? What'd you say?

11:58.660 --> 12:01.120
No. Sora is my friend.

12:01.120 --> 12:03.580
So, you'd rather go through 
something even more painful?

12:03.930 --> 12:08.210
Fine by me. Since you asked so nicely, 
I'll beat you to a pulp.

12:11.780 --> 12:12.790
Stop!

12:14.460 --> 12:15.710
You're not gettin' away!

12:22.690 --> 12:25.380
Pathetic. What are you doing?

12:28.100 --> 12:31.350
That little brat! 
He's not getting away with this!

12:35.980 --> 12:38.900
You've got a child's legs. 
Did you really think you'd escape?

12:41.630 --> 12:44.060
Which bag has the rare slime? Hand it over!

12:44.060 --> 12:45.790
No! Stop it!

12:45.790 --> 12:47.330
Stop struggling!

12:47.330 --> 12:49.600
Don't give us any trouble.

12:51.300 --> 12:52.780
Hey, what is it?

12:55.340 --> 12:57.630
A-Adandala!

12:59.570 --> 13:01.010
Ciel...

13:07.100 --> 13:08.520
She's so strong!

13:29.300 --> 13:32.540
Thank you, Ciel! You saved me!

13:33.260 --> 13:34.880
Are you all right, Sora?

13:37.080 --> 13:41.510
I wonder... When she caught the wild 
rabbits, did she do it like this?

13:42.940 --> 13:44.270
I sense more people.

13:44.270 --> 13:45.300
Ciel!

13:45.800 --> 13:47.460
Hey!

13:48.150 --> 13:49.640
That voice...

13:50.100 --> 13:51.940
Over here!

13:51.940 --> 13:54.590
Ivy! That was you?

13:55.720 --> 13:56.910
You're not hurt?

13:56.910 --> 13:57.690
No.

13:57.690 --> 14:01.890
As we patrolled the forest, we heard 
a monster's roar and human screams,

14:01.890 --> 14:03.410
so we hurried over.

14:03.780 --> 14:05.410
In that case, they're over there.

14:10.260 --> 14:13.050
About those four adventurers 
hassling you, Ivy...

14:13.050 --> 14:15.290
I looked into them, and they're 
all under investigation.

14:15.600 --> 14:17.260
Under investigation?

14:17.260 --> 14:22.150
They've been stealing money and goods from
young adventurers using false accusations.

14:22.150 --> 14:25.070
Their crimes were reported 
to the Adventurers Guild,

14:25.070 --> 14:27.260
but it was difficult to find 
evidence against them.

14:27.750 --> 14:29.260
I see.

14:29.260 --> 14:31.620
But there's something else I need 
to apologize about.

14:31.620 --> 14:32.140
What?

14:32.140 --> 14:33.910
The two we caught today...

14:33.910 --> 14:36.610
I've learned that they are wanted for murder.

14:36.610 --> 14:37.990
Murder?

14:37.990 --> 14:41.460
The two murderers will become slaves 
with no expectation of emancipation.

14:41.460 --> 14:44.690
The remaining two have been sentenced 
to long terms as slaves, too,

14:44.690 --> 14:46.640
so you won't be meeting them again.

14:46.640 --> 14:47.820
You can rest easy.

14:47.820 --> 14:50.130
Thank you so much.

14:50.130 --> 14:52.500
I've asked you here for a particular reason.

14:52.500 --> 14:57.750
As you helped in their capture, 
you're to be paid reward money, Ivy.

14:57.750 --> 14:58.880
What?

14:58.880 --> 15:01.840
The reward for an average
person is 5,000 dal.

15:01.840 --> 15:03.960
For a murderer, it's two gidal.

15:03.960 --> 15:07.970
For those two, the Guild offers 
a reward of one ladal each.

15:07.970 --> 15:11.110
So, all together, you'll receive 
two ladal and three gidal.

15:11.530 --> 15:13.560
<i>One field mouse is worth 100 dal,</i>

15:13.560 --> 15:16.400
<i>and one ladal is worth 
1,000 field mice.</i>

15:16.400 --> 15:20.670
<i>So, two ladal and three gidal 
is 2,300 field mice worth!</i>

15:20.670 --> 15:25.880
<i>The tip reward I received in Latom
was 2,800 field mice worth,</i>

15:25.880 --> 15:28.780
<i>so, all together, I have more than 
5,000 field mice worth!</i>

15:28.780 --> 15:30.550
This was quite the accomplishment.

15:30.550 --> 15:32.490
Ivy, have you made yourself an account?

15:32.810 --> 15:33.830
An account?

15:33.830 --> 15:36.320
Carrying around such a 
large sum must make you nervous.

15:36.320 --> 15:39.570
You can easily create an account 
at the Trade Guild.

15:39.920 --> 15:42.420
I'll be your guarantor. 
Let's go and deposit this.

15:47.310 --> 15:50.430
Please place one drop of blood here.

15:50.750 --> 15:55.390
There's a small needle in the depression. 
Please place your finger there.

15:55.390 --> 15:56.550
Yes, miss.

16:04.380 --> 16:05.690
Let's see what it says.

16:05.690 --> 16:06.960
"Name: Ivy."

16:06.960 --> 16:09.430
"Age: 8 years and 11 months." Wait!

16:09.430 --> 16:13.530
Ivy, you're turning nine soon?! 
I thought you were six or seven!

16:13.530 --> 16:15.450
I-I'm not that little!

16:15.450 --> 16:18.340
I mean, you're still little at eight...

16:36.930 --> 16:38.560
We have received your deposit.

16:40.590 --> 16:42.560
Thank you for using our services.

16:45.080 --> 16:49.110
With that plate, you can withdraw funds 
at the Trade Guild in any village or town.

16:49.110 --> 16:49.900
What do you think?

16:50.280 --> 16:53.490
<i>Huh? A "deposit book"?</i>

16:54.810 --> 16:55.540
What is it?

16:56.090 --> 16:58.610
It's nothing! Thank you!

16:58.610 --> 17:00.250
You've been a huge help!

17:01.650 --> 17:02.530
Don't worry about it!

17:02.530 --> 17:04.500
So, <i>this</i> is where you were?

17:04.500 --> 17:06.790
I've been looking for you, Captain.

17:06.790 --> 17:10.470
Please inform me as to where 
you are going before you leave.

17:10.470 --> 17:12.770
Oh, didn't I tell you?

17:12.770 --> 17:13.930
You did <i>not</i>!

17:18.080 --> 17:20.470
Ivy, have you eaten our signature dish here?

17:20.470 --> 17:21.310
Signature dish?

17:21.310 --> 17:24.770
Nonoshi skewers! I'll treat you, 
so eat as much as you want.

17:24.770 --> 17:25.660
What?

17:25.660 --> 17:28.730
<i>When was it decided that we'd eat together?</i>

17:28.730 --> 17:30.280
Let him treat you.

17:30.630 --> 17:32.240
Nonoshi is delicious.

17:32.240 --> 17:34.590
All right! I'm looking forward to it!

17:34.590 --> 17:36.070
I bet you are!

17:37.440 --> 17:41.710
<i>Now that I think about it, how long has it 
been since I've been patted on the head?</i>

17:41.710 --> 17:42.830
Is something wrong?

17:43.500 --> 17:46.540
No! I was just thinking 
that I'm getting hungry.

17:46.540 --> 17:48.630
I know a good spot. Let's go.

17:55.010 --> 17:56.560
Hey, shopkeep!

17:57.010 --> 17:58.790
Oh, Captain Oggto!

17:59.640 --> 18:00.770
A secret child of yours?

18:02.830 --> 18:04.280
Adorable, isn't he?

18:04.280 --> 18:05.730
Huh? What?

18:06.820 --> 18:09.070
Two beers and a noberry juice.

18:09.070 --> 18:10.150
Coming up!

18:11.360 --> 18:13.320
They're so big!

18:13.320 --> 18:15.960
Ten nonoshi skewers for each of us.

18:15.960 --> 18:16.770
Coming up!

18:16.770 --> 18:18.030
What? Ten?

18:18.460 --> 18:21.120
They're so good, 
it'll be easy to eat ten of 'em.

18:21.120 --> 18:22.580
I couldn't! I couldn't possibly!

18:22.580 --> 18:24.710
They're good, so just eat up!

18:24.710 --> 18:29.670
It isn't the flavor that's in question. 
Please consider Ivy's build, Captain.

18:30.760 --> 18:33.590
Don't stand on manners, just eat! 
Eat before they get cold!

18:33.590 --> 18:34.850
Eat as much as you want!

18:34.850 --> 18:35.550
Yes, sir!

18:40.650 --> 18:41.930
It's delicious!

18:41.930 --> 18:43.970
It's only natural that it's delicious.

18:43.970 --> 18:47.870
She's so skilled, no one would find it strange
should the royal capital ask for her food.

18:47.870 --> 18:52.030
You see, I have a four-star cooking skill.

18:52.480 --> 18:55.690
There aren't many who have a four-star skill.

18:57.490 --> 19:02.820
Speaking of which, the two we caught 
today both had three-star sprinting skills.

19:02.820 --> 19:04.870
It's no wonder it was so hard to catch them.

19:04.870 --> 19:09.340
The Watch could use more people 
with sprinting skills, couldn't it?

19:09.340 --> 19:12.340
Everyone's got skills suited for combat.

19:12.810 --> 19:15.320
Speaking of which, Ivy, what's your skill?

19:15.970 --> 19:17.530
Oh, yes.

19:17.530 --> 19:23.100
If your skill is a good fit, joining our 
Watch in the future might be a good idea.

19:24.370 --> 19:26.900
Ivy, what skill do you have?

19:26.900 --> 19:29.650
Um, I...

19:29.650 --> 19:31.570
I'm a tamer.

19:31.570 --> 19:33.860
A tamer? Well, that's wonderful!

19:33.860 --> 19:36.200
That's a skill which can help many people.

19:36.490 --> 19:38.920
So, how many stars does 
your tamer skill have?

19:39.260 --> 19:41.680
Well, um...

19:52.510 --> 19:53.940
It's all right.

19:53.940 --> 19:54.710
What?

19:55.500 --> 19:59.490
You see them sometimes, right? People 
with a lot of stars who are totally useless!

19:59.490 --> 20:01.610
Those thugs today were exactly that.

20:02.160 --> 20:03.180
Right?

20:03.180 --> 20:04.110
Indeed!

20:04.110 --> 20:07.010
Even with many stars, many people 
still fail to make use of their skill,

20:07.010 --> 20:09.520
and end up taking the wrong path in life.

20:09.520 --> 20:12.900
It is our job to keep 
such people under control.

20:13.820 --> 20:17.560
On the other hand, there are lots of 
praiseworthy people who have just one star.

20:17.560 --> 20:22.370
Yes, there are so many people who do 
wonderful work with their one star.

20:22.370 --> 20:25.700
So, Ivy, there's nothing to worry about.

20:25.700 --> 20:29.670
Ivy, you should be proud of yourself.

20:30.890 --> 20:32.070
I will.

20:37.540 --> 20:38.550
<i>I...</i>

20:39.320 --> 20:41.960
<i>I don't even have that one star.</i>

20:45.510 --> 20:47.480
I see. So, you're leaving.

20:47.480 --> 20:50.290
Yes. I promised the fortune teller,

20:50.290 --> 20:53.650
so I have to go to the town 
next to the royal capital.

20:53.650 --> 20:55.490
It's sad to see you go.

20:55.490 --> 20:58.000
If anything happens, just give them my name.

20:58.460 --> 21:02.370
If you say you're Oggto's friend, 
you can go wherever you want!

21:02.370 --> 21:03.760
I will!

21:03.760 --> 21:05.990
Thank you so much, truly!

21:08.900 --> 21:12.380
Come back one day! We'll be waiting for you!

21:12.380 --> 21:14.910
I will! One day, I'll come back!

21:19.360 --> 21:22.710
Captain, both the Adventurers Guild 
and the Trade Guild

21:22.710 --> 21:25.760
gave Latomi Village, the place 
where that child was born,

21:25.760 --> 21:28.180
a rank of 1, the lowest possible score.

21:28.180 --> 21:29.930
What about the list of people 
who left the village?

21:29.930 --> 21:32.360
I've checked them all,

21:32.360 --> 21:35.130
but the child's name wasn't on any of them.

21:35.130 --> 21:38.050
Most people left the village 
as whole families,

21:38.050 --> 21:41.950
but there was just one... one eight 
year old girl who ran away, alone.

21:41.950 --> 21:43.290
I see.

21:43.940 --> 21:46.090
So, the child has a secret.

21:46.090 --> 21:48.910
Some secret beyond hiding her gender.

21:48.910 --> 21:52.470
It must be the reason she 
couldn't stay in the village.

21:53.480 --> 21:56.250
I guess she couldn't 
bring herself to trust me.

21:56.250 --> 22:01.640
It just shows how deeply the events 
in Latomi have wounded her heart.

22:03.460 --> 22:05.970
One day, she'll tell you.

22:05.970 --> 22:09.600
Yes, one day. I'm certain of it.

22:11.000 --> 22:14.590
<i>You are not alone</i>

22:14.590 --> 22:18.150
<i>Open your eyes</i>

22:18.150 --> 22:19.940
<i>That’s the way</i>

22:19.940 --> 22:24.640
<i>You’ll be fine</i>

22:24.640 --> 22:28.720
<i>All of us are here now</i>

22:28.720 --> 22:34.540
<i>You’re something special</i>

22:34.540 --> 22:41.810
<i>Please just relax, and move forward</i>

22:42.800 --> 22:47.220
<i>Because you are here now</i>

22:47.220 --> 22:52.080
<i>The world is so beautiful</i>

22:52.080 --> 22:57.830
<i>This place is full of light</i>

22:57.830 --> 23:04.450
<i>You had countless nights of tears</i>

23:04.450 --> 23:11.840
<i>But you walked all the way here</i>

23:11.840 --> 23:18.160
<i>If it’s dark we’ll be your light</i>

23:18.160 --> 23:27.990
<i>You see the end of this road 
is crystal clear</i>
